{"sections": [
  {"key": "arc", "title": "The arc", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Revenue compounded at 34.8% a year from $404.5 million in FY2016 to $5,931.4 million in FY2025 [F1][F10][F196]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The shape is a decelerating ramp: growth ran 104.0% in FY2017 and 64.2% in FY2021, then fell to 0.1% in FY2023 and 10.6% in FY2025 [D36][D218][D311][D406]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "FY2017's operating loss of $3,485.6 million was driven by a $2.6 billion increase in stock-based compensation tied to the IPO-related RSUs and the CEO award [F12][P74]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The FY2022 reversal, with the operating loss widening 98.7% to $1,395.3 million, came from higher cost of revenue and operating expenses against only 11.8% revenue growth [F17][D264][D263][P42]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Since FY2023 the loss has narrowed every year, from -30.4% of revenue to -9.0% in FY2025, the best margin in the window [F28][F30][D554]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "drivers", "title": "What drove growth", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "North America still supplied the largest slice of FY2025 growth at +4.4pp of the 10.6% total, but its share of revenue fell to 58.6% from 81.9% in FY2017 [D458][D406][D456][D434]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Rest of world contributed +3.7pp on 17.0% growth and now is 23.0% of revenue, while Europe added +2.5pp [D499][D498][D497][D524]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Advertising revenue rose 5.8% to $5,186.1 million on roughly 17% more impressions, offset by a 10% lower cost per impression [S39][D537][P24]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Other revenue grew 62.9% to $745.4 million, now 12.6% of the total, on higher subscription revenue from subscriber growth [S42][D544][D543][P24]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating costs grew 5.1% against 10.6% revenue growth, so the incremental operating margin was 44.8% [D423][D406][D429]."}
  ]},
