    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The FY2025 operating margin of -9.0% is far above the -32.4% window median and the -422.5% low, but still 29.3pp below the 20.3% internet peer median [F30][D555][D553][D571]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Cost of revenue eased 1.1pp to 45.0% of revenue and R&D 1.3pp to 30.2%, while other lines added 3.3pp, lifting the margin 5.7pp [D386][D431][D387][D432][D433][D419]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Sales and marketing fell $42.4 million on the timing of marketing events and lower advertising, partly offset by higher headcount [X50][P22]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "R&D rose $101.9 million on product development and headcount, and G&A rose $60.0 million on external professional services including legal [X40][P23][X60][P21]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Net margin of -7.8% beat operating margin by 1.2pp, helped by $96.7 million of debt-extinguishment gains in other income [F50][F30][P18]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "cash", "title": "Cash conversion", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating cash flow of $656.2 million and free cash flow of $437.2 million both exceeded the $460.5 million net loss in FY2025, a 7.4% free-cash-flow margin [F80][F100][F40][D393]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The gap is non-cash: stock-based compensation of $1.0 billion and D&A of $163.6 million were added back to the net loss [P13][X90][X80]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Capex of $219.0 million was 3.7% of revenue and 1.34x D&A, up from 3.6% and 1.23x in FY2024 [F90][D392][D395][D344][D347]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Capex is mainly improvements to leased facilities to support team workspaces, not capacity expansion [P10]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "balance_sheet", "title": "Balance sheet and capital allocation", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Net cash swung from $1,439.8 million in FY2021 to net debt of $596.3 million in FY2025, -10.1% of revenue versus a 45.0% peer median [D211][D399][D400][D579]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Debt rose to $3,536.8 million as $1.4 billion of notes were repurchased and $1.50 billion of 2033 Notes issued in February 2025 [D398][P1][P2]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Liquidity is $2,940.6 million of cash and investments against a 3.56x current ratio, the window low [D397][F180][D565]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Buybacks of $750.9 million were 171.7% of free cash flow, and the diluted share count still rose 2.1% to 1,694.6 million [D401][D402][D425][X150]."}
